# MRW Multi-Root Workspace

When this workspace is opened via `mrw-multi.code-workspace`, you have access to two projects:

## radar-foundry (this project)

- **Radar products:** KCLX, KJAX, MRMS, satellite
- **Lightning products:** NexStorm, Xweather (hyper-local-x)
- **Master MRW Dashboard:** `player/master-mrw/`
- **Serves:** wx-i9:8080

## moonriverweather-public

- **Path:** `moonriverweather-public/` (or `/Volumes/Pierce_Archive/Cursor Weather Projects/moonriverweather-public`)
- **Purpose:** New moonriverweather.com public website
- **Consumes:** Products and data from radar-foundry, station data from pi-wx/api.moonriverweather.com

## Cross-project guidance

- **Data flow:** radar-foundry produces; moonriverweather-public consumes. When changing product schemas, endpoints, or URLs in radar-foundry, update moonriverweather-public if it uses them.
- **Shared concepts:** Lightning constants, station IDs, product URLs — see `docs/lightning/LIGHTNING_RULES_REFERENCE.md` and `docs/MRW_PROJECTS.md`.
- **Edit either project:** You can read and edit files in both folders. Use the folder name in paths when the target project matters (e.g. `moonriverweather-public/src/...`).
